 "library": {
  "title": "UiO-66-NH2 MOF unit cell, ball and stick",
  "description": "Amino-functionalised UiO-66 (UiO-66-NH2), the zirconium terephthalate metal-organic framework, as its full conventional cubic unit cell (Fm-3m, a = 2.07 nm), in nanometres. 488 atoms: Zr6O4(OH)4 clusters joined by 2-aminoterephthalate linkers, one NH2 per linker plus the ring hydrogens (OH hydrogens omitted). Ball-and-stick style: atoms at 0.6 x covalent radius, two-coloured half-bond sticks; Zr grey-blue, O red, C grey, N blue, H white. Lattice box hidden. Positions from the standard UiO-66 structure with NH2 and H placed geometrically (C-N 1.38, N-H 1.01, C-H 1.08 A); the NH2 sits on the same ring position in every linker (real material is disordered). Companion of the polyhedral UiO-66 MOF unit cell.",
  "tags": [
   "MOF",
   "UiO-66",
   "UiO-66-NH2",
   "zirconium",
   "Zr",
   "metal-organic framework",
   "ball and stick",
